                {
                    "file": "configurations/meta/harma/harma_fanboard.json",
                    "line": 573,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Patrick Williams",
                        "email": "patrick@stwcx.xyz",
                        "username": "williamspatrick"
                    },
                    "message": "Why do we have two devices both name \"Fan Board 1\", but one is the \"Upper\" and one is the \"Lower\"?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "configurations/meta/harma/harma_fanboard.json",
                    "line": 573,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "JunYe1993",
                        "email": "Daniel-Hsu@quantatw.com",
                        "username": "JunYe1993"
                    },
                    "message": "The system has two devices named \"Fan Board 1\" because of the mechanical design. The fan boards for the upper eight blades and the lower eight blades are installed in opposite orientations. Therefore, the \"Upper\" and \"Lower\" parameters are used to differentiate them."
                },
                {
                    "file": "configurations/meta/harma/harma_fanboard.json",
                    "line": 573,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Patrick Williams",
                        "email": "patrick@stwcx.xyz",
                        "username": "williamspatrick"
                    },
                    "message": "Can you confirm a system will only have one or the other installed then?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "configurations/meta/harma/harma_fanboard.json",
                    "line": 573,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "JunYe1993",
                        "email": "Daniel-Hsu@quantatw.com",
                        "username": "JunYe1993"
                    },
                    "message": "Yes, a system will only have one of them installed. From the BMC's perspective, it will probe either the Upper or the Lower fan board, as shown in the output below\n```\nroot@bmc:~# cat /var/configuration/system.json | grep BMC\\.Model\\.Harma\n            \"xyz.openbmc_project.Inventory.Source.DevicePresence({'Name': 'HarmaLowerFanBoard1', 'Compatible': 'com.meta.Hardware.BMC.Model.Harma'})\"\n            \"xyz.openbmc_project.Inventory.Source.DevicePresence({'Name': 'HarmaLowerFanBoard2', 'Compatible': 'com.meta.Hardware.BMC.Model.Harma'})\"\n                \"com.meta.Hardware.BMC.Model.Harma\"\n```"
                },
                {
                    "file": "configurations/meta/harma/harma_scm.json",
                    "line": 279,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Patrick Williams",
                        "email": "patrick@stwcx.xyz",
                        "username": "williamspatrick"
                    },
                    "message": "missing \"Model\"."
                },
                {
                    "file": "configurations/meta/harma/harma_scm.json",
                    "line": 279,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "JunYe1993",
                        "email": "Daniel-Hsu@quantatw.com",
                        "username": "JunYe1993"
                    },
                    "message": "Done"
                }
            ],
